CLONING:
============

Creating a copy of table:
1) Shallow Clone (only metadata is copied)
2) Deep Clone (copies both metadata and data)

create or replace table orders_mamnaged_sclone shallow clone orders_managed;
it will clone from latest version and contraints are also copied.

inserting new records at source has no impact on cloned table.
modifying data in cloned table, will create its own files and no impact to source table.

vacuum -> will delete only files which are not referenced.
drop source table-> data will not be deleted after 7 days and clone will not be impacted for 7 days in case of managed table.


1) Any changes made either to deep clone or shallow clone, affects only the clone itself and not source table
2) cloning a table is not same as CTAS as in CTAS constraints and descriptions are not copied.
3) shallow clones on external table must be external and on managed should be managed table.
4) for managed table, dropping source breaks the target table for shallow clone after 7 days. 
5) shallow clones on external table are not impacted on dropping source as files are not impacted.
6) clones can be taken for any version.

create table orders deep clone orders1 as of version 3;



DELTA UNIFORM:
===============

Read delta table with iceberg clients.
Parquet files remain same , it is the metadata that is diffierent.
While creating table we have to mention 3 properties.
1) 'delta.columnMapping.mode'  = 'name'
2) 'delta.enableIcebergCompactV2' ='true'
3) 'delta.universalFormat.enabledFormats' = 'iceberg'


describe formatted <table NAME>;


